; ============================================================================
; x.1sav.rtc.s3511a - the latched state of a Seiko S-3511A real-time clock
;
; An extension key for the Universal Saves Format, defined by these
; specifications under a name reserved in the Vendor Names registry because
; every emulator that keeps this clock keeps the same values.
;
; The root here is the value carried under the key, not a bundle. A bundle
; validates against the format's own schema whatever this holds, since an
; extension value is `any` there; this file is what makes the shape checkable.
; ============================================================================

rtc-s3511a = {
  0 => bstr .size 7,          ; components - latched BCD: year, month, day, weekday, hour, minute, second
  1 => uint,                  ; control    - the control register as read
  ? 2 => #6.1(int),           ; taken_at   - the producer's clock when it took the components
  ? 3 => bstr .size 2 / null, ; alarm      - the alarm register, as last written
}

; The alarm is absent when the game never sets it, and null when the game may
; have and the producer's source does not keep it. The chip reads the register
; back as all ones, so only a producer that saw the write holds it.

; 24-hour mode is bit 6 of the control register and does not get a field of its
; own. Two spellings of one value let a bundle contradict itself, which the
; format rules out everywhere else; see "One encoding per bundle".
